---
/**
 * The colophon line, carried over from pastey.io so the two sites sign off the
 * same way: "Made with ♥ and 🐿 in Kent, Ohio".
 *
 * Two things differ from the original, both because this site is themed and
 * that one is not:
 *
 *   1. The marks are inlined rather than served as `<img>`. Pastey ships them
 *      as two black-filled SVG files, which is fine on a page that is always
 *      light. Here the footer is dark by default and light by preference or
 *      toggle, so a fixed fill would go invisible on one of them. Inlined,
 *      they take `currentColor` and follow the paragraph — no second colour to
 *      keep in sync, and no two extra requests for 400 bytes of path data.
 *   2. They are sized in `em`, so they track the type ramp instead of being
 *      pinned at 18px. The heart lands on Pastey's 18px at the size this line
 *      is set; the squirrel is deliberately smaller, for the reason given
 *      against `.madewith__mark` below.
 *
 * The paths are the originals, unmodified: the heart is a clean 64-unit
 * drawing, the squirrel is a trace, which is why it keeps its `translate/scale`
 * wrapper and a 63-unit height.
 *
 * The marks stand in for words, so they are named rather than hidden —
 * `aria-hidden` here would have a screen reader say "Made with and in Kent,
 * Ohio". The names are Pastey's own alt text.
 */
---

<p class="madewith">
  Made with{" "}
  <svg
    class="madewith__mark"
    viewBox="0 0 64 64"
    role="img"
    aria-label="love"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <path
      fill="currentColor"
      d="M45.223,6A15.62,15.62,0,0,0,32,13.263,15.62,15.62,0,0,0,18.777,6,15.741,15.741,0,0,0,7.325,32.579L31.276,57.69a1,1,0,0,0,1.448,0L56.675,32.579l0-.005A15.741,15.741,0,0,0,45.223,6Z"
    ></path>
  </svg>{" "}
  and{" "}
  <svg
    class="madewith__mark madewith__mark--squirrel"
    viewBox="0 0 64 63"
    role="img"
    aria-label="squirrels"
    focusable="false"
  >
    <g transform="translate(0,63) scale(0.1,-0.1)" fill="currentColor">
      <path
        d="M50 612 c-27 -13 -37 -26 -44 -55 -14 -56 13 -80 99 -85 39 -3 65 -9 65 -16 0 -6 -25 -42 -54 -79 -97 -121 -93 -216 12 -324 47 -48 85 -56 242 -51 99 3 131 21 48 26 -27 2 -48 5 -48 7 0 3 9 19 20 37 11 18 20 49 20 70 l0 36 40 -5 c28 -4 50 0 81 16 25 13 51 20 64 17 14 -4 28 0 35 9 10 13 9 19 -6 36 -14 16 -25 19 -55 14 -20 -4 -39 -2 -43 3 -3 5 7 9 22 9 52 0 82 12 82 34 0 38 -28 86 -69 119 -23 18 -41 39 -41 47 0 26 -37 12 -61 -24 -28 -42 -85 -67 -136 -57 -32 6 -32 6 -18 35 39 75 -1 152 -96 182 -66 22 -115 21 -159 -1z"
      ></path>
    </g>
  </svg>{" "}
  in Kent, Ohio
</p>

<style>
  /*
   * A shade brighter than the fine print it sits beside (`--fg-3`) and a step
   * up in size, which is the relationship Pastey draws too: the sign-off is a
   * signature, the note next to it is a disclaimer.
   */
  .madewith {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-size: var(--t-small);
    line-height: 1.6;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /*
   * The sizes and offsets below are measured rather than guessed. At 14px this
   * face has a 7.1px x-height and a 10.1px cap-height, and the line is mixed
   * case, so both marks are centred on `baseline - 5px` — the optical middle of
   * a line that has capitals in it. That is what the two `vertical-align`
   * values work out to.
   *
   * The two drawings do not fill their boxes equally. The heart is inset about
   * a tenth of its viewBox on every side; the squirrel, being a trace, runs
   * edge to edge. Given the same box the squirrel draws 17.6px of ink against
   * the heart's 14.6px, which reads as a squirrel beside a much smaller heart.
   * The boxes below bring the ink to 15.4 and 14.6 instead — near enough level,
   * the squirrel left a shade taller because a standing figure carries less
   * weight than a solid shape at the same height.
   *
   * The margin is the gap Pastey gets from `mx-1`. Both marks sit close to
   * flush with their boxes, so the word space either side is not enough on its
   * own to keep them off the words.
   */
  .madewith__mark {
    /*
     * The reset in `global.css` puts every `svg` on `display: block`, which is
     * right everywhere else on the site — the other marks are all flex children
     * and the block avoids the inline descender gap. These two are glyphs in a
     * sentence, though, and a block one breaks the line on each side of it.
     */
    display: inline-block;
    width: 1.28em;
    height: 1.28em;
    margin-inline: 0.28em;
    vertical-align: -0.28em;
  }

  .madewith__mark--squirrel {
    width: 1.1em;
    height: 1.1em;
    vertical-align: -0.19em;
  }
</style>
